        rel="noopener">EDGAR full-text search</a> for Form D filings, issuer-name matched only —
        third-party SPV filings that merely carry a company's name are excluded. No Form D on
        record means no US exempt-offering disclosure, not no funding: many raises use
        exemptions that require no filing, and non-US companies rarely file.</p>
      {cpriv.companies.filter((c) => c.formd).length > 0 && (
        <>
          <h2>With SEC filings on record</h2>
          {cpriv.companies.filter((c) => c.formd).map((c) => (
            <div class="dom">
              <h3><a href={`${BASE}/${c.uid}/`}>{c.name}</a>
                <span class="n">{money(c.formd.sold)} disclosed</span></h3>
              <p class="meta-line">Most recent Form D{c.formd.amendment && ' (amendment)'}: filed
                {' '}{c.formd.filed} as {c.formd.issuer}, {money(c.formd.sold)} sold of a
                {' '}{money(c.formd.offering)} offering ·
                {' '}<a href={c.formd.url} rel="noopener">filing</a>
                {c.formd.filings > 1 && <> · {c.formd.filings} filings on record</>}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </>
      )}
      <h2>Tracked private companies</h2>
      <p class="chip-list">{cpriv.companies.filter((c) => !c.formd).map((c, i) => (
        <>{i > 0 && ' · '}<a href={`${BASE}/${c.uid}/`}>{c.name}</a></>
      ))}</p>
      <div class="cite-box">Cite this page: <code>"Private AI Companies." The World of AI,
        theworldofai.org{BASE}/{cpriv.uid}/. Retrieved {cpriv.generated}.</code></div>
    </>
  )}

  {corg && (
    <>
      <h1>{corg.name}</h1>
      <p class="answer"><b>{corg.total} {corg.total === 1 ? 'organisation' : 'organisations'}</b>,
        each individually verified against its own published materials — nothing here is
        classified by inference. {corg.blurb} Corporate research divisions (FAIR, DeepMind,
        Microsoft Research) live on their parent company's page rather than here.</p>
      <p class="meta-line">Last verified: {corg.generated} · This list is curated and grows as
        classifications are verified; a missing organisation is an editorial gap, not a
        judgement — <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>.</p>
      {corg.orgs.map((o) => (
        <div class="dom">
          <h3><a href={`${BASE}/${o.uid}/`}>{o.name}</a></h3>
          <p>{o.note.replace(/; source URL verified [0-9-]+$/, '')}.</p>
          <p class="meta-line"><a href={o.source_url} rel="noopener">Source</a> · verified {o.verified}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
      <div class="cite-box">Cite this page: <code>"{corg.name}." The World of AI,
        theworldofai.org{BASE}/{corg.uid}/. Retrieved {corg.generated}.</code></div>
    </>
  )}

  {cfund && (
    <>
      <h1>AI Funding: SEC Form D Disclosures</h1>
      <p class="answer"><b>{cfund.total} Form D filings</b> across <b>{cfund.companies} tracked AI
        companies</b>, newest first. A Form D is what a US company files when it raises money in
        an exempt offering — the closest thing to a primary source for private AI funding that
        exists free and lawfully. Each row is one filing: the amount reported sold at filing
        time, the offering size, and the document itself. Amounts are never summed across
        filings, because amendments restate the same offering.</p>
      <p class="meta-line">Last verified: {cfund.generated} · Source:
        {' '}<a href="https://efts.sec.gov/LATEST/search-index?q=%22test%22&forms=D" rel="noopener">SEC
        EDGAR full-text search</a>, issuer-name matched only. Valuations are not published here:
        no lawful free source for private-company valuations exists, and Form D does not disclose
        them. Absence from this list means no US filing on record, not no funding.</p>
      <table class="pay">
        <thead><tr><th>Company</th><th>Filed</th><th class="num">Sold</th><th class="num">Offering</th><th>First sale</th><th>Filing</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {cfund.filings.map((f) => (
            <tr>
              <td><a href={`${BASE}/${f.uid}/`}>{f.name}</a>{f.amendment && <span class="n">amend</span>}</td>
              <td>{f.filed}</td>
              <td class="num">{money(f.sold)}</td>
              <td class="num">{money(f.offering)}</td>
              <td>{f.first_sale || '—'}</td>
              <td><a href={f.url} rel="noopener">Form D</a></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="cite-box">Cite this page: <code>"AI Funding: SEC Form D Disclosures." The World
        of AI, theworldofai.org{BASE}/{cfund.uid}/. Retrieved {cfund.generated}.</code></div>
    </>
  )}

  {person && (
    <>
      <h1>{person.name}</h1>
      {person.tracked_only ? (
        <>
          <p class="lede">{person.title}{person.org && <>, {person.org}</>}</p>
          <p class="answer">
            {person.name} is tracked in the AI People Directory as {person.title} at
            {' '}{person.org}. <b>A full profile has not been written yet.</b> This page
            carries only what we have verified — the name, the role, and the organisation —
            rather than filling the gap with material we cannot source.
          </p>
          <p class="meta-line">Last verified: {person.generated}</p>
          <p>
            Profiles in this directory carry a timeline, achievements, and a source for every
            claim. When this one is written it will appear at this same address; the URL does
            not change. See the <a href={`${BASE}/${hubUid}/`}>full directory</a> for people
            who are already profiled.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
      {person.moniker && <p class="lede">{person.moniker}</p>}
      {person.hook && <p class="answer">{person.hook}</p>}
      <p class="meta-line">
        {person.nationality && <>{person.nationality} · </>}
        {person.born && <>Born {person.born}{person.died && <> · Died {person.died}</>} · </>}
        {person.generated && <>Last verified: {person.generated}</>}
      </p>

      {person.quote && <blockquote class="pq">{person.quote}</blockquote>}

      {person.fields?.length > 0 && (
        <p class="meta-line"><b>Fields:</b> {person.fields.join(' · ')}</p>
      )}

      {person.cats?.length > 0 && (
        <p class="meta-line"><b>Categories:</b>{' '}
          {person.cats.map((c, i) => (
            <>{i > 0 && ' · '}{c.uid
              ? <a href={`${BASE}/${c.uid}/`}>{c.name}</a>
              : c.name}</>
          ))}
        </p>
      )}

      {person.quick_facts && (
        <>
          <h2>Quick facts</h2>
          <table>
            <tbody>
              {Object.entries(person.quick_facts).map(([k, v]) => (
                <tr><th>{k.replace(/_/g, ' ')}</th><td>{Array.isArray(v) ? v.join(', ') : v}</td></tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </>
      )}

      {person.achievements?.length > 0 && (
        <>
          <h2>Known for</h2>
          <ul>{person.achievements.map((a) => <li>{typeof a === 'string' ? a : a.text || a.name}</li>)}</ul>
        </>
      )}

      {person.timeline?.length > 0 && (
        <>
          <h2>Timeline</h2>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Event</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {person.timeline.map((t) => (
                <tr><td>{t.year || t.date}</td><td>{t.event || t.text}</td></tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </>
      )}

      {person.sources?.length > 0 ? (
        <>
          <h2>Sources</h2>
          <ul class="cites">
            {person.sources.map((s) => (
              <li>{typeof s === 'string'
                ? s
                : (s.url ? <a href={s.url} rel="noopener">{s.title || s.url}</a> : (s.title || ''))}
                {typeof s !== 'string' && s.publisher && <> · {s.publisher}</>}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </>
      ) : (
        <p class="meta-line">This profile has no published sources attached yet. Treat the detail
          above as unverified until it does, and tell us if any of it is wrong:
          <a href="/contact/">contact</a>.</p>
      )}
        </>
      )}

      <div class="cite-box">Cite this profile: <code>"{person.name}." AI People Directory,
        The World of AI, theworldofai.org{BASE}/{person.uid}/.
        {person.generated ? ` Verified ${person.generated}.` : ''}</code></div>

      <p><a href={`${BASE}/${hubUid}/`}>All people</a></p>
    </>
  )}
</Base>

